   239\\\\t      return 0\\\\n   240\\\\t    fi\\\\n   241\\\\t    die \\\\\\\"$dest exists but is not a worktree of '$branch' (HEAD: ${have:-not a git worktree}); run 'git -C $ROOT worktree prune' or remove it\\\\\\\"\\\\n   242\\\\t  fi\\\\n   243\\\\t  mkdir -p \\\\\\\"$ROOT/.worktrees\\\\\\\"\\\\n   244\\\\t  git -C \\\\\\\"$ROOT\\\\\\\" worktree add --quiet \\\\\\\"$dest\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$branch\\\\\\\" ||\\\\n   245\\\\t    die \\\\\\\"git worktree add $dest $branch failed\\\\\\\"\\\\n   246\\\\t  if [ -x \\\\\\\"$ROOT/local/bin/worktree-setup.sh\\\\\\\" ]; then\\\\n   247\\\\t    \\\\\\\"$ROOT/local/bin/worktree-setup.sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$dest\\\\\\\" >&2 ||\\\\n   248\\\\t      warn \\\\\\\"worktree-setup.sh failed for $dest; the reviewer runs without a warmed build cache\\\\\\\"\\\\n   249\\\\t  else\\\\n   250\\\\t    warn \\\\\\\"local/bin/worktree-setup.sh not found; the reviewer worktree has no warmed Lean build cache (local/protocols/build-cache.md)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   251\\\\t  fi\\\\n   252\\\\t  printf '%s\\\\\\\\n' \\\\\\\"$dest\\\\\\\"\\\\n   253\\\\t}\\\\n   254\\\\t\\\\n   255\\\\t# run_agent <role> <sandbox> <worktree> <persona-path> <task-file>\\\\n   256\\\\t#           <standalone-prompt> <context-file> <out-file> <model>\\\\n   257\\\\t#\\\\n   258\\\\t# All codex invocations go through local/bin/dispatch.sh when it exists, so the\\\\n   259\\\\t# session lands in results/telemetry/sessions.jsonl (DESIGN.md, \\\\\\\"Agent\\\\n   260\\\\t# sessions\\\\\\\").  The fallback is a direct codex exec with a loud warning.\\\\n   261\\\\trun_agent() {\\\\n   262\\\\t  local role=\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\" sandbox=\\\\\\\"$2\\\\\\\" wt=\\\\\\\"$3\\\\\\\" persona=\\\\\\\"$4\\\\\\\" taskfile=\\\\\\\"$5\\\\\\\"\\\\n   263\\\\t  local standalone=\\\\\\\"$6\\\\\\\" ctx=\\\\\\\"$7\\\\\\\" out=\\\\\\\"$8\\\\\\\" model=\\\\\\\"$9\\\\\\\"\\\\n   264\\\\t  local dlog=\\\\\\\"$out.dispatch.log\\\\\\\" task_text last rc=0\\\\n   265\\\\t  task_text=\\\\\\\"$(cat \\\\\\\"$taskfile\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\"\\\\n   266\\\\t\\\\n   267\\\\t  if [ -x \\\\\\\"$DISPATCH\\\\\\\" ]; then\\\\n   268\\\\t    local args\\\\n   269\\\\t    args=(--role \\\\\\\"$role\\\\\\\" --issue \\\\\\\"pr$PR_NUM\\\\\\\" --pr \\\\\\\"$PR_NUM\\\\\\\"\\\\n   270\\\\t          --worktree \\\\\\\"$wt\\\\\\\" --sandbox \\\\\\\"$sandbox\\\\\\\"\\\\n   271\\\\t          --persona \\\\\\\"$persona\\\\\\\" --persona-ref \\\\\\\\\nlocal/bin/pr_merge.py:260:            f\\\\\\\"PR #{record.id} has review_state: null. Run local/bin/review.sh \\\\\\\"\\\\nlocal/bin/pr_merge.py:264:        check_review_verdict(record_dir, str(head_sha), str(review_state))\\\\nlocal/protocols/issues-prs.md:89:└── reviews/<sha>.md # one verdict per review, written by local/bin/review.sh\\\\nlocal/protocols/issues-prs.md:93:head_sha, ci_status, review_state, fix_iterations, auto_fix, labels, created,\\\\nlocal/protocols/issues-prs.md:226:4. `review_state: APPROVED`, or `COMMENTED` with zero unchecked findings in\\\\nlocal/protocols/issues-prs.md:227:   `prs/<id>/reviews/<head_sha>-*.md` (the verdict files `review.sh` writes:\\\\nlocal/protocols/issues-prs.md:245:`review_state: blocked` is a distinct refusal. Per DESIGN.md:66-69 a failed CI\\\\nlocal/bin/dispatch.sh:352:LAST_MESSAGE=\\\\\\\"$CAPTURE_DIR/$NAME.last.md\\\\\\\"\\\\nlocal/protocols/sessions.md:136:`results/telemetry/sessions/<name>.last.md`.\\\\nlocal/protocols/sessions.md:149:   next session needs. An empty `<name>.last.md` is reported as a warning by\\\\nlocal/protocols/sessions.md:176:and `<name>.last.md` are committed and never rewritten; the worktree is\\\\nlocal/protocols/sessions.md:295:| final message | `results/telemetry/sessions/<name>.last.md` | permanent, committed |\\\\nlocal/protocols/autofix.md:78:| — | unresolved findings in `reviews/*.md` **and** `auto_fix: true` | **review-fix** — `auto-fix-review-prompt.md` pair |\\\\nlocal/protocols/autofix.md:205:`fix_iterations` incremented, and `ci_status` / `review_state` reset to\\\\nlocal/protocols/autofix.md:278:| `prs/<id>/pr.md` | yes | `head_sha`, `fix_iterations`, `auto_fix`, `ci_status`, `review_state`, cap note |\\\\nlocal/bin/autofix.sh:615:      printf 'manifests under `ci/`, and the findings ledger under `reviews/`\\\\\\\\n'\\\\nlocal/bin/autofix.sh:804:  fm_set \\\\\\\"$PR_MD\\\\\\\" review_state pending\\\\nlocal/bin/pr_open.py:220:        \\\\\\\"review_state\\\\\\\": None,\\\\nlocal/bin/housekeeping.sh:259:    f\\\\\\\"review_state {pr.meta.get('review_state')!r}, \\\\\\\"\\\\nlocal/bin/track.py:528:    \\\\\\\"review_state\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fix_iterations\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"auto_fix\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"labels\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"created\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n./results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr0001-20260830-11.jsonl:473:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_244\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"## Findings\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:475` — `lem:qld-4-13` treats zero-direction evaluation classes as POVMs and drops the non-evaluating outcome mass.\\\\n- [ ] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:115` — `def:ld-meas` conflates polynomial representatives with the paper’s function-indexed outcomes for unrestricted `d`.\\\\n- [ ] F3 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:577` — `lem:twisted-commutation` uses a field element as an operator exponent and cannot derive the natural `p`-th power as written.\\\\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:606` — The proof incorrectly invokes `F_q`-linearity of `tr_{q→p}`, which is only `F_p`-linear.\\\\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:647` — `lem:pauli-observable-expansion` leaves the inversion parameter `b` unquantified.\\\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:380` — `lem:ortho` cites literal `[ML20]`, leaving its imported proof without a valid bibliographic reference.\\\\n\\\\n## Review\\\\n\\\\nChanges are required. This same-SHA re-review carries forward the six exact-head findings because the local protocol replaces that ledger. I found no additional code finding beyond the existing ledgers. The mathematical files are unchanged from the [previous code review](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/4277943db23d2dde26e90908ede8041fb7902e36-code.md:25), whose eight unresolved findings remain in force. The [exact-head prose review](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/b91e9bb01bd2e5f48a00a0750f53480e241b8576-prose.md:25) also remains unresolved.\\\\n\\\\n**F1.** `def:ideg-deg-polynomials` explicitly says that, on a zero-direction line, the classes indexed by `a ∈ F_q` form only a submeasurement and require an additional `⊥` outcome. Such lines occur with positive probability. Nevertheless, `lem:qld-4-13` applies POVM consistency to only the `F_q` classes, and the identity at line 927 similarly omits `⊥`. Complete the family or bound and absorb the missing mass. The source repeats this gap in `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1204`, label `claim:17-3`.\\\\n\\\\n**F2.** The source defines polynomials as reduced polynomial functions at `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:836` and uses function-indexed outcomes in `def:ld-meas` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:397`. The blueprint instead uses unrestricted formal representatives while `lem:ld-soundness` permits arbitrary positive `d`. Over `F₂`, `X` and `X²` are distinct representatives but the same function. Separate the paper-facing measurement class or restrict the identification to `d≤q−1`.\\\\n\\\\n**F3.** Both the source and blueprint write `(τ^W(a))^b` for `b∈F_p`, although operator exponentiation requires a natural or integer exponent. Moreover, substituting the field element `p=0` cannot establish the natural `p`-fold power. State the iteration law for `r∈N` using `(r mod p)·a`, then derive the `p`-th-power identity.\\\\n\\\\n**F4–F5.** The trace `tr_{q→p}` is `F_p`-linear, not `F_q`-linear; additivity is sufficient for the phase calculation. The Fourier inversion identity must also explicitly quantify `b∈F_q^n`, matching `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:1156`.\\\\n\\\\n**F6.** Replace literal `[ML20]` with the available `Ji2020LowIndividualDegree` citation key and identify the orthonormalization provider, whose proof begins at `references/ldt-paper/orthonormalization.tex:282`.\\\\n\\\\nI reviewed committed head `b91e9bb`; staged working-copy repairs were excluded and therefore do not resolve or outdate these findings. `git diff --check` is clean, no Lean source changed, and no direct proof hole or integrity bypass was introduced.\\\\n\\\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nresults/telemetry/sessions/orc-0007-implementation-continuation-20260831-01.jsonl:785:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_410\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"nl -ba local/bin/review.sh | sed -n '400,590p;700,790p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   400\\t  exit 0\\n   401\\tfi\\n   402\\tBRANCH_SHA=\\\"$(git -C \\\"$WORKTREE\\\" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)\\\"\\n   403\\tif [ -n \\\"$BRANCH_SHA\\\" ] && [ \\\"$BRANCH_SHA\\\" != \\\"$HEAD_SHA\\\" ]; then\\n   404\\t  log \\\"branch $BRANCH is at $BRANCH_SHA but GitHub head is $HEAD_SHA; exiting stale\\\"\\n   405\\t  exit 0\\n   406\\tfi\\n   407\\t\\n   408\\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- diff\\n   409\\tRUN_ID=\\\"$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)-$$\\\"\\n   410\\tRUN_DIR=\\\"$CACHE/review/$PR_NUM/$HEAD_SHA/$RUN_ID\\\"\\n   411\\tmkdir -p \\\"$RUN_DIR\\\"\\n   412\\t\\n   413\\tMERGE_BASE=\\\"$(git -C \