lueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md-74-F13. `def:ld-game` requires its dimension to divide `q`, but lines 898-906 instantiate it with `2m+2`; admissibility only gives `m | q`. For power-of-two `m≥2`, `2m+2=2(m+1)` has an odd factor and cannot divide power-of-two `q`. The same unsupported application occurs at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1278-1284`; a soundness theorem with a compatible sampler is required.
