results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr0001-20260830-01.last.md-41-F8. Source `def:graph-distribution` assigns equal mass `1/(2m-k)` to every ordered supported pair. Sampling an undirected edge uniformly and then orienting it assigns loops mass `1/m` and oriented nonloops mass `1/(2m)`, which differs whenever loops occur; this graph has a loop at every vertex. Sample uniformly from ordered support.
