results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md:23:**F1-F2.** Both scripts bind evidence to `HEAD_SHA` but execute against the live worktree without requiring it to be clean. An uncommitted repair can make CI pass for code absent from GitHub; dirty contextual files can similarly hide findings from a reviewer. Refuse dirty worktrees before publication, or use an isolated checkout of the exact SHA.
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-24-
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-25-**F3-F4.** CI marks only step contexts pending, while `review.sh` trusts the old `local-ci/summary=success`. Review rerequests are worse: `gh_common.post_review` keeps the old body, while `post_summary` merely warns on publication failure. An old approved body and green status can therefore survive a newly adverse review. Invalidate summaries with a fatal `pending` write before reruns, replace the published ledger, and make final status publication fatal.
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-26-
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-27-**F5-F6.** After waiting for the fix lock, `autofix.sh` rechecks only the remote head. A superseded run can leave a newer local commit unpushed, after which the waiter operates on that commit using the old head’s statuses and count. Separately, reaching the cap between phases invokes terminal review before the accumulated commit reaches GitHub, then exits without pushing it. Recompute local/remote state and the cap under the lock, and route cap completion through push, CI, then exact-head review.
--
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-31-**F8.** `/issues/N` also returns pull requests. Falling back after transport, authentication, or server failures can therefore classify a PR as an issue and select `main` for a write-enabled agent. Fall back only on a proven 404, and reject an issue response containing `pull_request`.
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-32-
results/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr7-20260901-01.last.md-33-**F9.** The regex misses `Closes: #42` and qualified same-repository references, while the gate scans no commit messages. GitHub documents all of these as closing surfaces, so a parent with open sub-issues can still be closed on merge. Expand both the parser and scanned inputs, with regression tests. See [GitHub’s closing-keyword syntax](https://docs.github.com/en/issues/tracking-your-work-with-issues/using-issues/linking-a-pull-request-to-an-issue?apiVersion=2022-11-28).
